      "content": "idk i get what ur saying about biology but it felt way too precise to be just a coincidence. like when i was looking at the candle formation, the way the volume spiked felt like it was responding to the specific way i was visualizing the frequency. if we talk about non-linear systems or how observer effects work in quantum mechanics, couldn't there be some kind of high-level feedback loop between a focused observer and a digital system that relies on probabilistic data? like maybe it's not 'moving' the market, but just tapping into the pattern already forming?",
